      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The relation of developing coronary artery disease risk factors to the taking a post were assessed. 5438 males aged 40-59 underwent the study. Significantly greater mean body mass, total cholesterol level, diastolic blood pressure and risk coefficient by Rose were stated in the group of office workers, whereas in the group of factory workers the percentage of overweighted men and smokers was significantly more frequently observed."},
